--
N5008 [class.mi]/4, [class.virtual]/2: the repeated base A is the second
(non-primary, Itanium C++ ABI 2.4) dynamic base of B and of C, so each of
D's A subobjects has a virtual pointer of its own; D::x overrides X::x in
both X subobjects; the implicit copy constructor copies both A subobjects
([class.copy.ctor]/14).  The front end rejected the class.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
